# Only the paths below need the owner's approval. Branch protection on master
# has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled with 0 required general
# approvals, so a PR touching only unlisted paths can be merged by its author,
# while a PR touching any path below cannot merge until a member of the `owners`
# team approves it. The team needs Write access to the repo or GitHub ignores it.
# Do not add a catch-all `*` rule: it would make every PR owner-gated again.
/.github/               @mitch-pro/owners
/tools/deploy.sh        @mitch-pro/owners
/AGENTS.md              @mitch-pro/owners
/rust/crates/mitch-lib/src/auth.rs @mitch-pro/owners

# Build and hosting: what production runs and how traffic reaches it.
/rust/Dockerfile        @mitch-pro/owners
/docker-compose.yml     @mitch-pro/owners
/caddy/                 @mitch-pro/owners
/SECURITY_POSTURE.md    @mitch-pro/owners

# Security gates: the global request gate (CSRF, auth checks), the admin
# passphrase, crypto helpers and the shared admin unlock client.
/rust/crates/mitch-server/src/handler.rs   @mitch-pro/owners
/rust/crates/mitch-lib/src/admin.rs        @mitch-pro/owners
/rust/crates/mitch-lib/src/crypto.rs       @mitch-pro/owners
/webserver/admin-auth.js                   @mitch-pro/owners

# Economy (see the "Economy integrity" rules in AGENTS.md).
/rust/crates/mitch-lib/src/coins.rs                    @mitch-pro/owners
